# INTENTIONALLY MINIMAL — package.json `files` is the source of truth.
#
# npm consults `.npmignore` only for paths that `files` did not already decide.
# This file used to duplicate the whole exclusion list (src/, examples/,
# tsconfig*, *.test.*), which read like the authoritative manifest while having
# almost no effect: `files: ["dist", ...]` already excludes everything not
# listed. Two manifests where one is dead is how a publish quietly ships the
# wrong thing.
#
# To change what gets published, edit `files` in package.json and verify with:
#   npm run check:manifest   (scripts/check-publishable-manifest.js, runs on prepack)
#   npm pack --dry-run
